# 003 — UI/UX Craftsmanship & Anti-Slop Directives

## 1. Visual Slop Prohibition
- DO NOT use flat `#000000` backgrounds with saturated neon accents (`violet-500`, `indigo-500`).
- DO NOT use multi-color continuous gradient text fills (`bg-clip-text text-transparent`).
- DO NOT use pulsing pill badges (`animate-ping`) or decorative emojis in component iconography.
- DO NOT use oversized diffuse glowing shadows (`blur-3xl`).

## 2. Design Tokens & Elevation
- Consume semantic tokens from `DESIGN.md` (`var(--surface-base)`, `var(--surface-raised)`, `var(--text-primary)`).
- Elevate components using 1px micro-borders and layered ambient shadows.

## 3. Motion & Animation Physics
- Never use generic `transition: all 0.3s ease`.
- Target exact animated properties (`transform`, `opacity`) with critically damped spring physics (`stiffness: 340, damping: 28`) or micro-times ($\le 150\text{ms}$).
- Wrap interactive animations in `prefers-reduced-motion` fallbacks.

## 4. Typography & Numerals
- Always apply `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums` (`.num`, `.tabular-nums`) to tables, financial amounts, counters, and dates.
